ATTRIBUTION CORRECTION. The subject describes a doc edit. The commit also
carries M2 part four of the device-grant certificate migration, swept off a
dirty tree while it was mid-verification.

Swept in:
  crates/system/session-runtime/src/wallet_grant/certificate.rs
    device_scope_certificate_path, device_grant_set_ref,
    save_device_grant_set, load_device_grant_set, and four tests
  crates/system/session-runtime/src/wallet_grant/mod.rs
    the re-exports for the above

That work is the storage seam the remaining flow switch depends on: the four
wallet flows read and write grants through one pair of calls, so they cannot
switch one at a time without leaving the tree reading one format while writing
another. Its account, including why the set needs its own content ref, is in
the following commit, "Record M2 part four: the storage seam".

This is the third such sweep in this migration (see also the notes on
1468e1b1 and f5951215, and commit 311b61a8 which named its sweep correctly).
No history surgery was done to un-bundle any of them: sweeping is the house
rule and is preferred to work sitting dirty. The defect each time is only that
the message did not say what was swept, which is what these notes repair.
